Files copied unchanged from osrep-unit-0.0.18.tar.gz:
  osrep_m6.pas         the API (encode/decode memory to memory, bounds, memory)
  osrep_encoder.pas    the encoder (-m6 = the long-range finder of osrep_lr.c)
  osrep_decoder.pas    the .osr decoder
  osrep_format.pas     the container (header, table, blocks)
  osrep_crc.pas        CRC-32C
  osrep_vhash.pas      VHASH-128 (the optional digest; PArc writes no digest)
  osrep_aes.pas        AES (used by the VHASH key schedule)
  osrep_lr.c           native -m6 long-range finder          (freestanding C, no libc)
  osrep_match.c        native match finder of the other methods
  osrep_vhash_nh.c     native VHASH NH
  osrep_crc_native.c   CRC-32C (SSE4.2 crc32 when present)
  README.md            the tarball's README
  LICENSE              MIT
  osrep-m6-api.md      docs/osrep-m6-api.md of the tag (Spanish; not in the tarball)

No change was needed: the units link the objects with plain {$L osrep_*.o}, which FPC finds
on the object path. The prebuilt objects of the tarball (obj/<target>/*.o; there is none for
darwin) are not vendored: build.sh compiles the four C files for every target with the
compiler of that target (README flags -O3 -fno-builtin -fno-stack-protector, plus
-ffreestanding and, with gcc, -fno-tree-loop-distribute-patterns, so no libc call is
generated). -dOSREP_NO_NATIVE uses the Pascal reference instead (same bytes; tests/srep.sh
checks it). Do not edit these files: update them from a new OSREP release.
